# Here are allowed (known) "derivational comment types".
#
# The syntax of a derivational comment of type DTYPE is
#   (DTYPE[0-9]+suffix)
# or
#   (DTYPE*reference)
# The reference is either explicitly provided as in
# the latter case, or in the former case it is formed
# from the lemma by removing the specified number
# of characters and appending `suffix`.
#
# For each derivational comment type, there are 3 possible values:
#
# - hidden: derivation comment type is allowed, but not visible in
#   the generated dictinary
#
# - visible_noninheritable: derivation comment type is visible in
#   the generated dictonary, but only for the unchanged lemma
#   (i.e., it is not inherited by automatically derived lemmas)
#
# - visible_inheritable: derivation comment type is visible in
#   the generated dictonary and is inherited by automatically
#   derived lemmas

^DD*  visible_inheritable

*     hidden
